# ti.msp432p401r.blink_uart_demo
# Real, hand-written (no vendor SDK/generator - see target.toml) bare-metal
# P1.0 + EUSCI_A0 demo for TI MSP432P401R, the fifth TI chip under this
# plan. See ../../../../../replica-server/renoly_examples/ti/msp432p401r/README.md.

using sysbus
mach create "MSP432P401R_Blink_UART_Demo"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platform.repl

# Bare @$ORIGIN/firmware.elf, not a path reflecting the local build-output
# layout - REQUIRED, not stylistic. server/bundle.py's materialize_bundle
# only literal-string-replaces exactly that bare form when staging an
# uploaded bundle for the real client -> StartSession/RunSimulation path;
# anything else resolves fine for local direct-parse testing but silently
# fails to load over the real deployed path - see
# renoly_examples/st/stm32l476/README.md's own real incident with this
# exact mistake, avoided here from the start. A synced flat firmware.elf
# copy lives at this demo's own root (sibling to this file).
sysbus LoadELF @$ORIGIN/firmware.elf

# EUSCI_A0 TXBUF write watchpoint - observes the boot marker as it's
# transmitted (real, timing-independent proof it actually ran). "[Tag]
# Description" convention (see server/session.py's
# WatchpointHook.label/description) - is_byte_tap (chr(value) matches)
# routes this to Bus Traffic, matching every other UART-touching example
# in this repo, not Events. The numeric width field (4) is parsed but not
# enforced by this engine's own watchpoint dispatch (fires on any write
# to this exact address, regardless of the real access width the CPU
# used) - kept at 4 to match every other example's own convention, not
# because this register is actually 32-bit (it's real 16-bit eUSCI_A -
# see hw/ti/msp432/eusci.py's own docstring).
sysbus AddWatchpointHook 0x4000100E 4 Write "print(chr(value & 0xFF), end='')"

# DIO Port A OUT-register write watchpoint, masked to the real P1.0 bit -
# register-level proof the blink loop genuinely toggles the pin, not just
# that main() didn't fault. Not a byte-tap -> lands as a real, labeled
# [DIO] Event.
sysbus AddWatchpointHook 0x40004C02 4 Write "print('[DIO] P1.0 write value=0x%X' % (value & 0x1))"

start
